{
  "about": "On-device check for live video (the explicit-content blocker): the runtime and the models. Every file is pinned by SHA-256; the page fetches it from the GifOS model host at <base>/<key>, checks every byte and hands the bytes to the check's worker, which makes no request of its own. src names the published file the copy was taken from. chain: every sampled frame goes to the first model; a frame goes on to the confirming model only while the first finds it at or over its line, and counts as explicit only when the confirming one does too. The confirming model is Freepik EVA02, chosen per device at run time: gpu (the fp32 build on WebGPU, only on a desktop whose browser passes the self-test below: the probabilities for made-up pictures must match the reference machine within tol, and a frame must take under maxMs, half the 0.9 s the int8 build takes on one WebAssembly thread of a desktop) else the chain's second stage (the int8 build on WebAssembly). fuse: the keep/lift fit of that model, s = a*logit(m) + b*g(f) + c (see gifos-explicit.js fuseScore); confirm: the score under which a confirming look counts as clean. Score = the sum of the pos classes of the softmax. A GPU that fails is remembered on the device for rememberMs (a week), so its download is not repeated.",
